cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DockScreen in your work, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "DockScreen: SMILES preparation and batch molecular docking"
version: "0.3.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Karkhanin"
    given-names: "Kirill V."
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  DockScreen prepares ligands from SMILES and performs CPU docking screens
  against prepared receptors using an external AutoDock Vina executable,
  with bounded CPU allocation, calculation caching and CSV/JSON/HTML exports.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - molecular docking
  - virtual screening
